{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/768337-kith-and-seeming-and-mien-oh-my","id":768337,"title":"Kith and Seeming and Mien Oh My!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T00:55:37-08:00","id":768337,"title":"Kith and Seeming and Mien Oh My!","content":"So I've been thinking about the 2e Changeling Mien and I'm a little confused about the descriptions in the kith in conjunction with the descriptions in the seeming as they relate to the Changeling's mien. And I think I'm missing something because I don't understand something. If a Changeling's seeming isn't decided until they escape then how does their seeming factor into the way that they look as dictated by their kith? How does a Beast Blood Brute end up looking like a scar ridden predator if she wasn't a Beast until she snapped? How are the Chatelaine Fairest and the Wizened differentiated until they've left?<br /> <br /> I understand that the Gentry will craft the Changelings to suit their needs - Manikins are going to be like dolls or robots, Polychromatics are going to be rainbow decorations of humans. But what if when they leave their durance they're Beasts? Is there an animalistic overlay to the robot? Does the rainbow turn into multicolored fur? <br /> <br /> ETA: And also when specifically does that happen? Because the difference in the mien between say a Riddleseeker Beast and Wizened is like a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8367-mascaria","user":"mascaria","date":". 11-18-2015, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8367-mascaria","name":"mascaria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8367_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T05:34:46-08:00","id":768434,"title":"","content":"Your mien changes when you escape Arcadia. <br /> <br /> In Arcadia you might take the form of a literal dragon, a giant lizard with wings, green scales, breathing fire.<br /> <br /> Then you escape in a way that lets say makes you a fairest and your form shifts.<br /> <br /> You'd shink down to your former size, regain your humaniod shape, and your seeming would twist your remaining dragonic features.<br /> <br /> Maybe your scales would take on a metallic golden colour, both beautiful and majestic, instead of your old green scales.<br /> <br /> If you became a darkling instead maybe your scales would turn black and leak tendrils of shadowstuff into the air.<br /> <br /> This isn't the end of the changes, ones mien changes when one joins a court to reflect that court, and changes again when one achieves a higher court mantle.<br /> <br /> Also if entitlements are a thing they also produce changes in ones seeming.<br /> <br /> And possibly high wyrd can cause changes to ones mien, at least in the last edition it did.<br /> <br /> So basically you mien can mutate under specific situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-18-2015, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:30:56-08:00","id":768749,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the clarification! I think for some reason I was thinking of the mien as fixed after the Changeling has left the Hedge, forgetting that it still changes as situations do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8367-mascaria","name":"mascaria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8367_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:13:09-08:00","id":769418,"title":"","content":"The mein is a mix of flesh and glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}